# the song store after the official firmware: V16's image writes over the pool's first 36 KB and
# leaves SiDJ's entries beyond it. The walk at boot stops at the overwritten start (no songs), and
# songs added then must not pick the old entries up again, not even when one ends exactly where an
# old entry starts (the first here: 4064 bytes + its header fill one sector)
songraw 4064
songraw 1000
songraw 1000
expect songs 3
poolwrite 0 0x800 0x5a
reboot
expect songs 0
songraw 4064
expect songs 1
songraw 1000
expect songs 2
reboot
expect songs 2
